From: LEVY%BESSIE@venus.cis.yale.edu
Date: Sun, 23 Jan 1994 18:35:21 -0500 (EST)
Subject: [#94-1-440] LEGAL: Announcement of PPL1 Policy

List Members,

As Harry has recently announced, I am now the head of PPL1, the ExI PPL, to 
which most of you belong.  This change should cause little or no disruption in
anyone's life. Still, I think it is appropriate for me to make known my
intended policies.  In brief, I will pursue a simpler form of justice than
Harry did. I will be taking three actions to maintain a high S/N ratio:

(1) Scanning the List for flames, basics-debating, ad-hominem (or -feminam)
    arguments, and other types of nasty behavior mentioned in the Welcome
    message.  If I detect such behavior, I will send a single *private* 
    warning to the offending party.  If the behavior continues, I will 
    implement what I consider an appropriate punishment (suspension from the 
    List for some period of time).  If I consider the behavior especially 
    egregious, I will skip the warning and implement a punishment immediately. 
    If the perpetrator is not in PPL1, I will initiate *private* negotiations 
    with the perp's PPL.  (If you haven't received Harry's approval for creation
    of a new PPL, you are in PPL1 by default.)

(2) Listening to charges, which must be sent to me *privately*.  I will ignore 
    charges posted to the List and will consider the annoyance caused thereby 
    to nullify the charges themselves.  If A brings charges against B, I will
    decide whether B's post contains a violation of List etiquette.  If I find 
    no such violation, I will notify A *privately* that I find no violation.
    I will discourage A from bringing similar charges in the future, and I will
    eventually punish A if A continues to annoy me with bogus charges.  If,
    however, I agree that B has behaved inappropriately, I will notify
    B *privately* and give B 24 hours to respond.  As I intend to punish *all*
    violations, regardless of "who started it", the only relevant information
    that B could give me would be some inappropriate behavior on the part of A,
    in which case I will take action against A as well; I will take action
    against B regardless of B's response.  I think that this system discourages
    both intiation of flames and response to them.  If either A or B is not a 
    member of PPL1, I will initiate *private* negotiations with the head of the 
    other PPL. If neither A nor B is a member of PPL1, I will of course not 
    listen to charges from either.  

(3) Ejecting extreme offenders (Pandit Singh types) from the List.  Like all
    of my judgements, ejection will be done at my discretion, and I will not
    discuss the matter with those whose advice I have not solicited.

My goals are twofold:  I wish to implement swift justice, and I wish to keep
legal issues off the List.  For the latter reason, you will not see any 
"Charges have been filed against... " messages from me on the List.  If I
take action (suspension or, more rarely, ejection) against somone, I will
announce the action *after* taking it, along with my reason. The announcement 
should be construed as an attempt to convey information about the kind of 
behavior I consider actionable, and *not* as an attempt to initiate
discussion about legal issues in general or about my judgement in particular.
Furthermore, to prevent "hit and run" maneuvers, ExI will not accept a PPL
formation request from anyone during the period in which I am taking action
against that person (from the intiation of charges to the end of the suspension
period).

Also, please be aware that ExI is considering the PPL system provisionally;
if it ends up a failure in our eyes, we will replace it with something simpler
(like a single List "referee" who has sole authority).  For example, if we 
find that troublemakers are starting their own one-person PPLs as a basis for
flame-launching, we will probably shut down the PPL system  (or we will use our
ownership of the List as the basis for ejecting the offender). The next couple 
of months will determine whether ExI considers List PPLs a success or not.  

To conclude, I would like to thank Harry for doing double duty in the legal
and technical management of the List.  As he stated in an earlier message,
ExI considers it enough work for anyone to be doing either of these jobs,
so we are shifting the burden of legal matters to my shoulders, and leaving
the technical burden on Harry's.  This means that Harry is no longer the
person to talk to about legal matters.  Complaining to him about a judgement
will have no effect other than annyoying both him and me.

Finally, here's a bit of advice for PPL1 members, from the Ren & Stimpy 
show, which conveys rather nicely my views about List etiquette:

		*** DON'T WHIZ ON THE ELECTRIC FENCE ***


Please address any questions about these matters to me *privately*.  I will
not answer such questions if you post them to the List.

