From: Harvey Newstrom <hnewstrom@hnewstrom.ess.harris.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Jan 94 19:55:40 EST
Subject: [#94-1-444] GOAL:  Save time

Any other activities that waste time that we can try to reduce besides 
sleep?  TV is a biggie.  I watch about four shows per week.  I never watch 
them live, I always tape them and skip the commercials.  I can watch an 
hour show in 45 minutes this way.  Eating often gets in my way.  I 
sometimes mix a protein/nutrient shake when I am too busy working to eat 
properly.  Three meals a day takes a lot of time.  So does cooking.  I have 
already thought of (but not implemented) the idea of skipping lunch at work 
so that my workday is shorter.  I could drink a nutrient shake and work 
through, and go home earlier.  Although I haven't done this yet, this seems 
worth it to me.

I already pay someone to mow my lawn.  I have a food service that delivers 
the basic foods.  (I only shop for specific items as I desire.)  I shift my 
work schedules so I go in 15 minutes after the rush instead of 15 minutes 
before.  This alone cuts my commute time in half, depending on what time I 
go to work.  (My total commute is now only 15 minutes.)

I don't want to sound obsessed with efficiency, however.  The human body 
and mind requires relaxation.  The purpose of saving time is to get more 
work done and have more free time.  Anybody working 100% of the time will 
experience diminishing returns.
__
Harvey Newstrom  (hnewstrom@hnewstrom.ess.harris.com)


